There seems to be a small mistake in your code. In the `.then()` block, you're trying to log the response, but there's a syntax issue. Here's the corrected version:

```javascript
axios.get("https://swapi.dev/api/people/1/")
  .then(res => {
    console.log("The response is", res);
  })
  .catch(error => {
    console.error("There was an error!", error);
  });
```

- I fixed the URL (`swapi.dev` instead of `swapi.defev`).
- The `.then()` block now correctly logs the response (`res`), using a comma rather than concatenating strings with a dot (`.`).
- I added a `.catch()` block to handle errors, which is always a good practice when dealing with asynchronous code.

Let me know if you need any more adjustments!
